---
import ArrowIcon from "../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import evidenceManifest from "../../manifests/rights-and-sources.v1.json";
import routeManifest from "../../manifests/route-actions.v1.json";

const publicLocation = (location: string) => location.startsWith("https://") ? location : undefined;
---

<BaseLayout title="Transparency" canonicalPath="/transparency" description="Ownership, sources, rights, route policy, corrections and unresolved evidence for ai-fanout.com.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Transparency</h1>
    <div class="page-head-copy">
      <p>Ownership, methods, evidence gaps and corrections belong beside the work—not in a hidden footnote.</p>
      <p class="meta-line">Manifest · {evidenceManifest.manifestVersion} · reviewed {evidenceManifest.reviewedAt}</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="ownership section-pad section-rule" aria-labelledby="ownership-title">
    <div><span class="section-number">01</span><h2 id="ownership-title" class="section-title">Ownership &amp; independence</h2></div>
    <div>
      <p>{site.ownershipDisclosure}</p>
      <p>Contextter and SEO Fanout may later consume a user-controlled export, but shared ownership never turns either site into independent validation. ai-fanout.com must remain useful without those links.</p>
      <p>ai-fanout.com was newly registered by Matthias Ramahi for this project. Matthias is the operator and Research Owner: he versions the tool and method, records corrections, states reviewer status and owns the EUR 25 soft / EUR 30 hard monthly cost envelope.</p><p>No independent reviewer or provider benchmark is claimed. OpenAI and Gemini Native Fanout are live behind CAPTCHA, per-bucket and site-wide quotas, an atomic monthly budget ledger and a separate public enable flag.</p>
      <p>The server keeps no raw topic or provider response. Results are stored only when a visitor explicitly saves them in IndexedDB on that device. OpenAI observations can retain visible queries, action-linked sources and usage data. Gemini saves strip Google Grounded Results and Search Suggestions before writing query strings and run metadata locally. History is limited to 20 entries and 30 days, has visible deletion controls, is not synchronized and is not a shared response cache.</p>
      <p>Dated public examples contain owner-run OpenAI observations only. The public OpenAI-vs-Gemini page is a comparison protocol, not a retained Gemini transcript, because Google places additional restrictions on Grounded Results and Search Suggestions.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad section-rule" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
    <span class="section-number">02</span><h2 id="sources-title" class="section-title">Verified source register</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">A source supports only the statement named here. Owner records, primary documentation, standards and live technical checks remain distinct evidence roles.</p>
    <ol class="source-register ruled-list">
      {evidenceManifest.sources.map((source) => (
        <li>
          <span>{source.checkedAt}</span>
          <div><h3>{source.title}</h3><p>{source.supports}</p></div>
          <div><strong>{source.status.replaceAll("_", " ")}</strong>{publicLocation(source.location) ? <a href={source.location} rel="external">Open source <ArrowIcon size={16} /></a> : <small>Local or central record</small>}</div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="rights section-pad section-rule" aria-labelledby="rights-title">
    <div><span class="section-number">03</span><h2 id="rights-title" class="section-title">Rights decisions</h2></div>
    <dl>
      {evidenceManifest.rights.map((right) => (
        <div><dt>{right.assetClass}</dt><dd><strong>{right.status.replaceAll("_", " ")}</strong><p>{right.decision}</p></dd></div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="routes section-pad section-rule" aria-labelledby="routes-title">
    <div><span class="section-number">04</span><h2 id="routes-title" class="section-title">Current route policy</h2></div>
    <div>
      <p>This is a fresh registration. The route manifest describes only the current product and normal unknown-path handling.</p>
      <dl><div><dt>Sitemap source</dt><dd>{routeManifest.sitemapMode.replaceAll("_", " ")}</dd></div><div><dt>Excluded routes</dt><dd>{routeManifest.excludedFromSitemap.join(", ")}</dd></div><div><dt>Unknown paths</dt><dd>{routeManifest.defaultUnknownPathAction}</dd></div><div><dt>Catch-all redirect</dt><dd>{routeManifest.catchAllRedirect ? "Enabled" : "Disabled"}</dd></div></dl>
      <p>Canonical English and German 200 pages are indexable and discovered through an automatically generated sitemap. The operational tracker remains noindex. Retired comparison and research routes, and all other unknown paths, return a real 404.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="unknowns section-pad section-rule" aria-labelledby="unknowns-title">
    <div><span class="section-number">05</span><h2 id="unknowns-title" class="section-title">Still unknown</h2></div>
    <ul>{evidenceManifest.unknowns.map((unknown) => <li>{unknown}</li>)}</ul>
  </section>

  <section class="corrections section-pad" aria-labelledby="corrections-title">
    <div><span class="section-number">06</span><h2 id="corrections-title" class="section-title">Corrections &amp; contact</h2></div>
    <div><p>For a factual, rights or methodology correction, email <a href="mailto:info@matthiasramahi.de">info@matthiasramahi.de</a> or open a public issue in the source repository and name the affected route and evidence. Do not post vulnerabilities, credentials, private endpoints or personal data publicly.</p><a class="text-action" href={site.githubUrl} rel="external">Open the source repository <ArrowIcon /></a><p>Security concerns use GitHub private vulnerability reporting as described in <code>SECURITY.md</code>.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ownership, .rights, .routes, .unknowns, .corrections { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.7fr 1.3fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 8rem); }
  .ownership > div:last-child, .routes > div:last-child, .corrections > div:last-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .ownership p, .routes p, .corrections p { max-width: 62ch; margin: 0; padding-block: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fine-rule); line-height: 1.65; }
  .source-register { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .source-register li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem minmax(0, 1fr) 11rem; gap: 1.5rem; padding-block: 1.25rem; }
  .source-register > li > span { font: 0.72rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); }
  .source-register h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .source-register p { margin: 0.45rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  .source-register li > div:last-child { display: grid; align-content: start; justify-items: start; gap: 0.65rem; }
  .source-register strong, .source-register small { color: var(--signal); font: 0.68rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .source-register a { display: inline-flex; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: center; font-size: 0.76rem; }
  .rights dl { margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .rights dl > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.7fr 1.3fr; gap: 1.5rem; padding-block: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fine-rule); }
  .rights dt { font-weight: 600; }
  .rights dd { margin: 0; }
  .rights dd strong { color: var(--signal); font: 0.68rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .rights dd p { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .routes dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .routes dl > div { padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--fine-rule); border-left: 0; }
  .routes dt { color: var(--muted); font: 0.66rem/1.3 var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .routes dd { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; font: 1rem/1.3 var(--font-mono); }
  .unknowns ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); list-style: none; }
  .unknowns li { position: relative; padding: 1rem 0 1rem 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fine-rule); }
  .unknowns li::before { position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--signal); content: "?"; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .corrections .text-action { margin-top: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 780px) { .ownership, .rights, .routes, .unknowns, .corrections { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .source-register li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.6rem; } .rights dl > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .routes dl { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .routes dl > div { border-left: 1px solid var(--fine-rule); border-bottom: 0; } }
</style>
